PLANNED COMMIT: fixup into 1f6f3310 (CDM byte-budget commit). Message paragraph to add:
  "A walk does not check again the last page it found good, for a program or for an indirect
  launch's 12 argument bytes, and it makes at most 16384 page checks; one more is refused as
  'CDM page check budget'. The walk holds no device lock: the queue's mutex covers the SUBMIT,
  and the VM's lock is taken per check (about 4 us on the J516C) and per 256-byte read (about
  5 us). Before this, a stream of 24-byte indirect launches with distinct argument pages made
  one check per launch, about 0.8 s per compute command and about 51 s per 64-command SUBMIT;
  now it is at most about 149 ms per command and about 9.5 s per SUBMIT. Mesa's indirect
  arguments move to a new page every few dispatches: 40000 dispatches made 41410 checks in
  224 ms before and 6848 in 94 ms after, and the largest stream the link budget admits (47000
  dispatches) makes 8047. The 608 dEQP-VK multi_draw.mosaic max_draws with_tess cases pass."
  Plus the host-test lines for the three new cases.

